From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: allixender <alexander.kmoch@ut.ee>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 09:36:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] DgProjISEA: inverse latitude by atan2, no pole snap

snyderInv() computes sinlat and takes asin(sinlat), which is
ill-conditioned at +-1: near a pole it loses half the digits (ca 1e-8 rad
with a 53-bit long double). 9.2 added a snap to the pole when
1 - |sinlat| <= 4 * LDBL_EPSILON. Where long double is double (macOS
arm64, Windows arm64) that snap radius is ca 2.4e-6 deg (27 cm), larger
than the cells at the pole from ISEA res 17 on. All their vertices snap
onto the pole, the new dropDuplicatePoints() in DgIDGGBase then removes
the duplicates, and GENERATE_GRID writes the pole cells of IGEO7v2 /
IGEO7v1 with 5 vertices at res 17 and a single point at res 18-20
(9.1: 6). x87 (snap radius 5e-8 deg) and quad builds don't show it.

The direct problem from the face centre has all three components of the
point: sin(lat), cos(lat) sin(dlon) = sin(azh) sin(z) and
cos(lat) cos(dlon) = cos(lat0) cos(z) - sin(lat0) sin(z) cos(azh).
lat = atan2(sin(lat), hypot(..)) and lon = lon0 + atan2(..) are well
conditioned everywhere, no snap needed. The coslon expression it
replaces is the same quantity, simplified.

With double long double: pole cells res 15-20 have 6 vertices again in
all four IGEO7 / IVEA7 presets, the res 18 north pole cell is within
1e-5 m of the x87 build (9.1 double: up to 6 cm). examplesNoGDALorH3:
all outputs unchanged except hiRes/littleTri27.shp (res 27, coordinates
differ by up to 2.8e-14 deg).
---
 src/lib/dglib/lib/DgProjISEA.cpp | 37 +++++++++++---------------------
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 24 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/lib/dglib/lib/DgProjISEA.cpp b/src/lib/dglib/lib/DgProjISEA.cpp
index 19bd4441..a598c98e 100644
--- a/src/lib/dglib/lib/DgProjISEA.cpp
+++ b/src/lib/dglib/lib/DgProjISEA.cpp
@@ -22,7 +22,6 @@
 //
 ////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
 
-#include <cfloat>
 #include <cmath>
 #include <climits>
 
@@ -241,7 +240,7 @@ GeoCoord snyderInv (const IcosaGridPt& icosaPt, SphIcosa& sphicosa)
 */
 {
   long double ddazh,ph,fh,azh,azh1,dazh,h,fazh,flazh,dz,z;
-  long double sinlat,sinlon;
+  long double sinlat;
   long double azh0;
   GeoCoord Geovect;
   const PreCompGeo& cent = sphicosa.triCen[icosaPt.triangle];
@@ -306,31 +305,21 @@ GeoCoord snyderInv (const IcosaGridPt& icosaPt, SphIcosa& sphicosa)
     while (azh > M_PI_L) azh -= M_2PI;
 
     sinlat=cent.sinLat * cosl(z) + cent.cosLat * sinl(z) * cosl(azh);
-    if (sinlat > M_ONE) sinlat = M_ONE;
-    if (sinlat < -M_ONE) sinlat = -M_ONE;
-    Geovect.lat = asinl(sinlat);
-
-    // asin is ill-conditioned at +-1: sinlat within a few units in the last
-    // place of +-1 (here 0.5 ulp gives 3e-10 radians) puts the point closer
-    // to the pole than this formula resolves, and the longitude computed
-    // below would be a ratio of rounding errors. Snap it to the pole.
-    if (fabsl(fabsl(Geovect.lat) - M_PI_2_L) < M_EPSILON ||
-        M_ONE - fabsl(sinlat) <= 4.0L * LDBL_EPSILON)
-    {
-       Geovect.lat = (Geovect.lat > M_ZERO) ? M_PI_2_L : -M_PI_2_L;
+    // The point from the face centre (direct problem) with all three of its
+    // components: sin(lat) above, cos(lat) sin(dlon) and cos(lat) cos(dlon).
+    // atan2 is well conditioned everywhere; asin(sinlat) is not near the
+    // poles, where it loses half the digits (ca 1e-8 rad in double) and
+    // needed a snap that moved whole pole cells onto the pole there.
+    const long double clsl = sinl(azh) * sinl(z);
+    const long double clcl = cent.cosLat * cosl(z) -
+                             cent.sinLat * sinl(z) * cosl(azh);
+    const long double cl = hypotl(clsl, clcl);
+    Geovect.lat = atan2l(sinlat, cl);
+    if (cl == M_ZERO)
        Geovect.lon = M_ZERO;
-    }
     else
     {
-      sinlon = sinl(azh)*sinl(z)/cosl(Geovect.lat);
-      long double coslon = (cosl(z) - cent.sinLat * sinl(Geovect.lat)) /
-              cent.cosLat/cosl(Geovect.lat);
-      if (sinlon > M_ONE) sinlon = M_ONE;
-      if (sinlon < -M_ONE) sinlon = -M_ONE;
-      if (coslon > M_ONE) coslon = M_ONE;
-      if (coslon < -M_ONE) coslon =-M_ONE;
-      Geovect.lon = cent.pt.lon+asinl(sinlon);
-      Geovect.lon = cent.pt.lon+atan2l(sinlon, coslon);
+      Geovect.lon = cent.pt.lon + atan2l(clsl, clcl);
       if (Geovect.lon <= -M_PI_L) Geovect.lon += M_2PI;
       if (Geovect.lon >= M_PI_L) Geovect.lon -= M_2PI;
     }
